אני רק מ打通告诉你 everything already got resolved  Wait, I need to translate the Chinese sentence into Hebrew. Let me think again.  The Chinese sentence is: 我只是打电话告诉你一切都已经得到了解决  Breaking it down: - 我 (wǒ) = I - 只是 (zhǐshì) = just/only - 打电话 (dǎ diànhuà) = to call (on the phone) - 告诉你 (gàosù nǐ) = to tell you - 一切 (yīqiè) = everything - 都 (dōu) = all/already - 已经 (yǐjīng) = already - 得到了 (dé dào le) = has been obtained/received (in this context, it's used to indicate completion) - 解决 (jiějué) = resolved/solved  So the sentence means: "I'm just calling to tell you that everything has already been resolved."  Now, translating this into Hebrew:  "אני מתקשר רק כדי להודיע לך שכולו כבר נפתר"  Let me break down the Hebrew translation: - אני (ani) = I - מתקשר (mitkales) = am calling - רק (rak) = just - כדי (kidmi) = in order to - להודיע (lehodi'ah) = to inform - לך (lach) = to you - ש (she) = that - כולם (kolam) = everything (literally "all of them", but in this context it means "everything") - כבר (kvar) = already - נפתַּר (niftar) = has been resolved (from the verb פתר, which means to solve/resolve)  So the final translation is: "אני מתקשר רק כדי להודיע לך שכולו כבר נפתַּר"
